course: dictionary
lesson: 5758
title: Luck and chance
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Luck is when good or bad things happen by chance, not because of what you did. «Maddie's ball gets chewed to shreds by the neighbour's Staffie.» Maddie did nothing wrong, so this is bad luck, and her mum says «Tough luck, love.»
explain: Good luck is when chance goes your way, and bad luck is when it does not. Read the words around luck to tell which one it is. «Some folk are like that, pet» shows that Maddie's mum is sorry for her, so the luck was bad.
explain: Some games are won by thinking, like chess, and some are won by luck, like a simple dice game. In a game of chance nobody is to blame for losing. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: if «bad luck» fits, it is chance and not someone's fault.
fact: Luck means good or bad things happening by chance, not because of what you did.
fact: «Good luck!» is said to wish someone success.
fact: Probability is the maths of luck: it tells you how likely something is to happen by chance.
fact: Black cats and broken mirrors do not really bring bad luck. That is a myth, not a fact.
fact: Phrases with luck include by luck, in luck, out of luck, try your luck and beginner's luck. Read the words around them to work out the meaning.
exercise: «Maddie's ball gets chewed to shreds by the neighbour's Staffie.» Is this good luck or bad luck? | Good luck | *Bad luck | A lucky number | Nobody's luck at all
exercise: «Good luck!» is said to do what? | Ask for money | Say goodbye to someone | *Wish someone success | Make a ball bounce
exercise: In a game of chance, who is to blame for losing? | The player who lost | *Nobody | The referee | The dice, always
test: Which game is won by luck rather than thinking? | Sudoku | *A simple dice game | Chess | Chess and draughts
test: Which of these is a myth, not a fact? | Good luck wishes someone success | Probability is the maths of luck | Luck is chance | *Black cats really bring bad luck
exam: Which phrase wishes someone success? | Beginner's luck | Out of luck | *Good luck! | Bad luck
